  abstract = {This paper develops a model of the interbank network in which unsecured claims and obligations, repo activity and shocks to the haircuts applied to collateral assume centre stage. We show how systemic liquidity crises of the kind associated with the interbank market collapse of 2007-8 can arise within such a framework, with contagion spreading widely through the web of interlinkages. And we illustrate how greater complexity and concentration in the …nancial network may contribute to fragility. We then suggest how a range of policy measures –including tougher liquidity regulation, macro-prudential policy, and surcharges for systemically important …nancial institutions – may make the …nancial system more resilient.},
